      body: "The Privacy Protection Study Commission, created by the Privacy Act of 1974, transmitted 'Personal Privacy in an Information Society' to President Jimmy Carter on 12 July 1977. Congress had asked it to recommend how far the Privacy Act's principles should apply to organisations other than federal agencies; its chapters covered credit, banking, mailing lists, insurance, employment, medical care and other record-keeping relationships. It proposed three objectives for national policy, the first 'to create a proper balance between what an individual is expected to divulge to a record-keeping organization and what he seeks in return'.",
