      body: "Overnight on 16–17 November 1984, Steffen Wernéry and Wau Holland of the Chaos Computer Club logged into the Deutsche Bundespost's new Bildschirmtext (Btx) service with the Hamburger Sparkasse's ID and password and had a program call a CCC page priced at DM 9.97 13,504 times, a virtual DM 134,634.88. The club had written to data-protection officials and the Bundespost about flaws in October 1984; after the hack its press release called for a ban on financial transactions on Btx. The 'bank robbery' made the CCC famous overnight.",
