      body: "On 11 January 1996 Assistant U.S. Attorney William Keane in San Jose told Zimmermann's lawyer, Philip Dubois, that Zimmermann would not be prosecuted over the June 1991 Usenet posting of PGP, ending a three-year investigation. U.S. Attorney Michael J. Yamaguchi announced that his office had declined prosecution of any individuals and gave no reasons. Dubois speculated the government may not have wanted to risk a ruling that posting software on a US Internet site is not an 'export', or that the export-control law was unconstitutional.",
