      body: "David Goldschlag, Michael Reed and Paul Syverson of the U.S. Naval Research Laboratory, who had begun the work in late 1995, presented 'Hiding Routing Information' at the Workshop on Information Hiding in Cambridge, UK, in May 1996. Their 'onion routing' architecture relayed traffic through proxy servers so that no one but the initiator's proxy knew more than the previous and next hop, and a prototype already worked with web (HTTP) proxies. The design built on David Chaum's layered mix of 1981.",
