      note: "The United States has no comprehensive federal data-privacy law. The Privacy Act of 1974 (signed 31 December 1974, in force 27 September 1975) governs federal agencies' records only; the private sector is covered by sectoral statutes (credit, health, children, video rentals and others). The first comprehensive state law was the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018, since followed by many other states. There is no general federal privacy regulator; the FTC polices unfair and deceptive practices.",
