      contribution: "Barlow, a Wyoming rancher and Grateful Dead lyricist who met the 'electronic frontier' on the WELL, co-founded the Electronic Frontier Foundation with Mitch Kapor and John Gilmore in 1990 after the Secret Service raid on Steve Jackson Games. On 8 February 1996, the day the US Telecommunications Act (with its Communications Decency Act) became law, he wrote in Davos 'A Declaration of the Independence of Cyberspace', rejecting government sovereignty over the online world. He died on 7 February 2018.",
      influence: "By Barlow's own count the declaration was on at least 10,000 websites within a month and became the reference text of internet exceptionalism; twenty years on he conceded that the self-regulation it promised had, 'in most ways', not arrived, and EFF has defended him against the charge of naive techno-utopianism.",
