          title: "Networked Privacy",
          date: "2011-06-06",
          url: "https://www.danah.org/papers/talks/2011/PDF2011.html",
          quote: "Privacy is a feeling that people have when they feel as though they have two important things: 1) control over their social situation; and 2) enough agency to assert control.",
          note: "Same talk: 'Privacy isn't about the individual's relationship to information. If we want to have privacy in this world, we need to think about what networked privacy looks like.' The page calls itself a 'VERY rough unedited crib of the actual talk'.",
