      contribution: "At the University of Texas, Shmatikov co-authored the Netflix Prize de-anonymisation with Arvind Narayanan and, with him, a 2010 Communications of the ACM essay arguing that 'personally identifiable information' is a poor basis for privacy protection because any distinguishing detail can re-identify someone. In 2016-17 he co-authored a membership-inference attack on machine-learning models, showing that a model's outputs can reveal whether a given record was in its training data. He is a professor at Cornell Tech.",
